            <ArticleTitle>The thiazolidinediones: a new class of antidiabetic agents.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>185-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Insulin resistance is a fundamental feature of type 2 diabetes and is strongly associated with metabolic disorders which predict increased cardiovascular risk, including hypertension and dyslipidaemia. A new class of insulin-sensitizing agents, the thiazolidinediones, reduce insulin resistance and improve glycaemia both as monotherapy and in combination with sulphonylureas or metformin.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
